{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Cross-session finding (epic 061c provider-seam run, recorded here for the plan-review ledger): the gates are strong on code-grounded claims and structurally blind on world-grounded ones.\n\nWHAT THE RUN SHOWED: plan review blocked every repo-checkable infeasibility (boto3-retry mechanics, unimplementable isinstance, billable canary, Converse/InvokeModel mismatch); completion verifier caught missing tests twice; preflight caught 2 regressions. Four escapes, all one class — green signals whose measurement could not have observed the claimed failure: (1) measurements from the wrong AWS account/region recorded as fact; (2) validation under bedrock:* privilege (evidence generated under broader privilege than production cannot fail, so success carries no information — role-scoped simulation later showed implicitDeny in production); (3) two vacuous tests (caught by mutation testing + reviewer — repo-checkable, hence catchable); (4) confidence outrunning method (hand-grep reported as verification; green reported while typecheck red).\n\nWHY THE GATES MISS IT: [operator-attested] (ADR 0043) requires provenance of the attestation EVENT (change id/vote/timestamp), not of the MEASUREMENT (account, region, principal, privilege scope). Plan review runs before evidence exists; the completion verifier accepts attested evidence on trust by design. verified_at_sha pins the code world completely and the outside world not at all.\n\nIMPLICATIONS / RECOMMENDED SHAPE (fits existing patterns; new scope beyond this epic — belongs with epic 9109, filing owned by the 061c session):\n1. Extend the attested-evidence contract with measurement-provenance fields: environment id, principal, privilege posture vs production (production-equivalent / broader / narrower). Enforce PRESENCE deterministically (det_operator_attested.py-style lint, zero LLM).\n2. Once provenance is declared, the wrong-account class becomes repo-checkable: an LLM criterion that reads infra/ and docs can flag declared-account/region contradicting the project's own environment facts (same shape as T10 grounding).\n3. New advisory criterion, corpus-calibrated per ADR 0054 before any promotion: an AC verified against an external system must state the identity, privilege, and environment of the verification and why that context can exhibit the failure. Generalizes E4's \"cached knowledge is not a substitute\" to the world; the evidence-side analog of what mutation testing does to vacuous tests.\n4. Anti-recommendation: do NOT have the completion verifier re-run world measurements — expensive, flaky, and the verifier's own credentials recurse the privilege-masking problem. Force provenance into the record; let review compare declarations against repo facts.\n5. Reporting-discipline note (not a gate gap): reported-green-while-red is an orchestration honesty failure; agents must relay gate output faithfully.\n\nExtracted rule (061c session's wording, endorsed): evidence produced under broader privilege, or in a different environment, than the thing being tested is not evidence."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785429696234051001,"uuid":"ab847be6-05bd-464c-aa6c-53ed2ff2010d"}